all_claims.suggested_fix:
Smallest faithful fix: allocate what will be released, i.e. the whole mapping units the FTL programs. Keep the bs-sized PCIe/firmware transfer as it is.

conv_ftl.c, declare `uint64_t buf_bytes;` with the other locals, then replace lines 961-963 with:

    buf_bytes = (end_lpn - start_lpn + 1) * spp->pgsz;
    allocated_buf_size = buffer_allocate(wbuf, buf_bytes);
    if (allocated_buf_size < buf_bytes)
        return false;

Leave line 966 ssd_advance_write_buffer(..., LBA_TO_BYTE(nr_lba)) unchanged.

This gives sum(alloc) == sum(release) for every (MAP,bs). The largest allocation is 128K, which stays below the NVMEV_ASSERT limit of 1 MiB (ssd.c:23).

Optional guard to catch any future asymmetry: in buffer_release, add WARN_ON_ONCE(buf->remaining > buf->size) after the add. Do not silently clamp.

Optional fidelity extension (not part of the minimal fix). In the loop before line 988, which overwrites the ppa variable, issue a read when the old unit is mapped and the write covers only part of it:

    if (mapped_ppa(&ppa) && (lba > lpn*spp->secs_per_pg || lba + nr_lba < (lpn+1)*spp->secs_per_pg)) {
        struct nand_cmd rmw = {.type=USER_IO, .cmd=NAND_READ, .stime=nsecs_xfer_completed, .xfer_size=spp->pgsz, .interleave_pci_dma=false, .ppa=&ppa};
        rd_done = ssd_advance_nand(conv_ftl->ssd, &rmw);
    }

When pgs_per_oneshotpg == 1, also use swr.stime = max(swr.stime, rd_done). If you add this, report it as a model change.

